-- Ordered quest guidance; source 967020b2b8ca645afcaf90d9bbe5a1b64673947d; generated 2026-10-20.
QuestGuidance.Register("en",158,{
[5025]="7001AACC\n1\tDefeat Sharpfang\tSharpfang may be found at Hrigg Vidukuni, west of the Wild Ruins, south-west of Ost Galadh. Fuirgam has asked you to travel to Hrigg Vidukuni and search the area for the Emyn Lûm pack-leader, Sharpfang, and defeat him.\n2\tTalk to Fuirgam at Ost Galadh\tFuirgam at Ost Galadh is at Ost Galadh, north of the Wild Ruins, north-east of Hrigg Vidukuni. You should return to Fuirgam with news of your success.\n",
[5026]="70046C2C\n1\tQuestion Daugha-tûm\tDaugha-tûm can be found in Aelin Veren, in central North Ithilien. Maendal has asked you to question the Haradrim prisoners, beginning with the warrior Daugha-tûm.\n2\tTalk to Maendal\tMaendal can be found at Aelin Veren. You and the Rangers were forced to slay a rebelling Haradrim prisoner. You should talk to Maendal about what is to be done.\n",
[5027]="7002EF81\n1\tCollect Warg-fangs\t\n2\tTalk to the mysterious old man at Éomer's Vengeance\030Collect Warg-fangs (total: 8)\tWargs can be found at Thrug-unur, north-east of Éomer's Vengeance in the Entwash Vale. You should defeat as many Wargs as you can to further aid the cause of Thane Béortnoth and the survivors of Thornhope. Their fangs would make a good trophy to prove your success.\n",
[5028]="70008822\n1\tSpeak with Lieutenant Sturla at Lugazag\030Collect Wintersebb-fangs (total: 5)\tDrakes can be found in Arador's End to the north and east of Lugazag. Lieutenant Sturla asked you to retrieve drake fangs to assist in the crafting of arrows for the war effort and reinforcement of Lugazag.\n",
[5029]="7002BFF7\n1\tCollect wild cat fangs (total: 6)\tWild cats can be found throughout the Brown Lands and at the Khundolar encampment of Lashkarg, south-east of Etheburg. Twiga has asked you to hunt the wild cats of the Brown Lands and bring him their fangs as a testament of your valour.\n2\tBring the wild cat fangs to Twiga at Etheburg in the Brown Lands\tTwiga is at Etheburg in the Brown Lands, north-west of Lashkarg. You should bring the fangs you collected to Twiga as a token of your valour.\n",
[5030]="7003466F\n1\tDefeat wolves in the Whitshaws (total: 10)\tWolves can be found throughout the Whitshaws. You should defeat the wolves that have come in across the frozen plains.\n2\tCompleted\tYou have defeated a number of wolves in the Whitshaws, but they will return, as long as the unnatural winter holds fast. As long as wolves roam, hunters are needed.\n",
[5031]="70058745\n1\tDefeat Wargs upon the battlefield (total: 10)\tWargs can be found upon the battlefield. You should defeat any Warg you find upon the battlefield.\n2\tCompleted\tDefeated many Wargs upon the battlefield.\n",
[5032]="7005B4A7\n1\tCollect mist-walker pelts (total: 6)\030Collect sabre-tooth fangs (total: 8)\tClovengap mist-stalkers and sabre-tooth cats can be found in the vineyards. Nósni has asked you to bring back furs from Clovengap mist-stalkers and fangs from the deadly sabre-tooth cats of Clovengap.\n2\tReturn to Nósni\tNósni is in Hagbuth in north-east Clovengap. Bring the furs and fangs to Nósni.\n",
[5033]="70028244\n1\tTalk to Bedwur to raid the outpost outside the Wulf's Cleft encampment\tBedwur is in Avardin in the central Starkmoor. Bedwur has asked you to travel to an overlook of Wulf's Cleft and destroy whoever comes to find you.\n2\tTalk to Bedwur in Avardin\tBedwur is in Avardin in the central Starkmoor. Bedwur will be pleased to hear you have secured a large profit for him from the forces at Wulf's Cleft.\n3\tTalk to Eva in Avardin\tEva is in Avardin, in the central Starkmoor. Eva may have knowledge of where the boy has gone.\n",
[5034]="700395D5\n1\tBurn banners of the White Hand\tBosa's Farm can be found to the east of Middlemead in northern Kingstead. You have discovered the ruined remains of Bosa's Farm and should burn the White Hand banners you discovered.\n2\tBurn banners of the White Hand (total: 6)\tWhite Hand banners can be found scattered about Bosa's Farm to the east of Middlemead. Uruks of the White Hand have laid claim to Bosa's Farm. You should burn their banners to aid in loosening the White Hand's grip on Kingstead.\n3\tCompleted\tYou have burned many banners of the White Hand and erased the Uruks' claim to Kingstead's lands.\n",
[5035]="7003FFF7\n1\tFood secured (total: 3)\tThe food stores must be saved.\n",
[5036]="70019C4C\n1\tTalk to Raingon\tRaingon is at Talan Gwilith. You should speak with Raingon to prepare the defences for battle.\n2\tFanuidhol attackers defeated ([see journal]/30)\tRaingon has asked you to defeat the attackers out of Fanuidhol at both Talan Gwilith and Talan Fanuidhol, while protecting the Elven soldiers.\n3\tRaingon is at Talan Gwilith. With the assault turned aside, you should speak with Raingon.\t\n",
[5037]="70041216\n1\tTalk to the Master of Horses in the Cave of the Avorrim\tThe Master of Horses is in the Cave of the Avorrim. Dorthaneth has asked you to speak to the Master of Horses, who cares for the swiftest Avorrim horses.\n2\tBorrow the swift horse from the Master of Horses and ride to the Dead Marshes\tThe Master of Horses cares for a swift horse in the Cave of the Avorrim. Dorthaneth wants to fulfill the wishes of Lady Galadriel, and has asked you to borrow a fast horse from the Master of Horses and carry out an important errand in the Dead Marshes.\n3\tTalk to Artamir at his camp in the Dead Marshes\tArtamir, son of Ilcamir, has come to the Dead Marshes on an errand, but Galadriel of Lórien fears his presence there may draw unwanted attention to those lands.\n",
[5038]="7004185E\n1\tTalk to Melawen\tMelawen can be found in Malbarth in western Lebennin. Barchir has asked you to speak with the people of Malbarth before you depart for the east.\n2\tTalk to Lendithil\tLendithil can be found in Malbarth in western Lebennin. Barchir has asked you to speak with the people of Malbarth before you depart for the east.\n3\tTalk to Arvaeth\tArvaeth can be found to the north-west of Malbarth in western Lebennin. Barchir has asked you to speak with the people of Malbarth before you depart for the east.\n",
[5039]="70047BE6\n1\tThe Wainrider chieftain can be found somewhere within Dol Acharn. Disturbing an object of his people might rouse him to step forth from the shadows. Faramir has asked you to draw forth and defeat the Wainrider chieftain in the hope you might gain an audience with him.\t\n2\tTalk to Chieftain Zhan Ashû at Dol Acharn\tChieftain Zhan Ashû can be found atop Dol Acharn in eastern Dagorlad. You have bested the chieftain in combat and he now wishes to speak to you. You should attempt to convince him of the Bloodletter's danger to his people.\n3\tTalk to Faramir near Dol Acharn\tFaramir can be found due west of Dol Acharn in Dagorlad. You have told the Wainrider chieftain of the Bloodletter's heritage and of the banner he bears, but his people still remained hostile despite their apparent gratitude. You should return to Faramir.\n",
[5040]="700571EF\n1\tWave good-bye to Madelgard Túcca\030Wave good-bye to Heldric Túcca\030Wave good-bye to Ogiva Túcca\030Wave good-bye to Vilihad Túcca\030Wave good-bye to Valaric Túcca\030Wave good-bye to Odger Túcca\030Wave good-bye to Erma Túcca\030Wave good-bye to Ubbo Bolga\030Wave good-bye to Gísla Bolga\030Wave good-bye to Badehild Bolga\030Wave good-bye to Fastrada Túcca\030Wave good-bye to Clodar Túcca\030Wave good-bye to Húbald Túcca\tThe Holbytlan can be found in Lyndelby. You should wave good-bye to the Holbytlan you have met with today.\n2\tLeave Lyndelby\tYou should travel over the old stone bridge and leave Lyndelby.\n3\tTalk to Fanglind near Lyndelby\tFanglind can be found near Lyndelby. You should talk to Fanglind.\n",
[5041]="700681A0\n1\tTalk to Berkha\tRaghda-gûn has realized she may not be best suited to care for little Berkha, and has arranged for you to take him with you. Speak to Berkha at Raghda-gûn's nest, Aklâradum, atop a cliff south of Halrax.\n",
[5042]="700630E1\n1\tTalk to Murig\030Talk to Deryn\030Talk to Marget\tEluna has asked you to say farewell to her students before you leave. Talk to Murig, Deryn, and Marget.\n2\tTalk to Eluna\tEluna is waiting for you. Talk to Eluna.\n",
[5043]="7004178F\n1\tJoin Faltharan as he says his good-byes\tFaltharan can be found at the steps to Tol Ciryarani. Speak with Faltharan to head to the shipyard.\n2\tTalk to Faltharan\tFaltharan can be found at the steps to Tol Ciryarani. You should speak with Faltharan.\n",
[5044]="7003A664\n1\tSpeak with Calin\tCalin is on the first floor of the farmhouse, and is looking into arranging a search party for the missing farmers.\n2\tInvestigate the farm-fields\tThe farmers have gone missing, and are suspected to be out in the fields somewhere.\n3\tThe fields are disturbed by someone who has no regard for the crops. This was clearly not the farmer's doing. It does not bode well for the missing farmers.\t\n4\tSpeak with Herubrand\tHerubrand should be told of the farmers being murdered so close to where he is hiding.\n5\tSpeak with Gifemund\tSpeak with Gifemund about the security concerns in the city. He has taken over the protection for Woodhurst, and it is clear that things have not gotten better.\n6\tReturn to Herubrand\tReturn to Herubrand in his hideout within the farmhouse cellar and tell him of Gifemund's promise to keep the fields watched.\n",
[5045]="70062036\n1\tSearch for the woodworking tools\tCendrew Hove has asked you retrieve his woodworking tools from his farm. The Hove family farm is in Cardolan.\n2\tRecover stolen tools (total: 6)\tYou found the farmer's toolbox, but it was empty. You suspect that the goblins who have infiltrated the farm carried off the tools. You should defeat goblins at the Hove farm and recover the stolen tools. The Hove farm is located in north-central Cardolan.\n3\tReturn to Cendrew\tYou should bring the woodworking tools back to Cendrew Hove. Cendrew is at the Scurloc farm in north-eastern Cardolan.\n",
[5046]="70007804\n1\tCollect produce from Asphodel Froghorn\tThe Widow Froghorn's farm is on the road west and south of Eldo Swatmidge's farm. Eldo Swatmidge asked you to collect the produce that Asphodel Froghorn means to sell.\n2\tBring the basket of vegetables to Himloc Grouse\tHimloc Grouse can usually be found in the town square of Staddle, west of the Widow Froghorn's farm. Asphodel seems to think highly of you and has asked you to sell some of her produce to Himloc Grouse, the trader.\n3\tBring Himloc's payment to Asphodel Froghorn\tWidow Froghorn's farm is east of Staddle. Asphodel Froghorn is waiting for the payment you received from Himloc Grouse for the sale of her vegetables.\n",
[5047]="70025DE0\n1\tTalk to Hob Hillbrow in Dwaling\tHob Hillbrow is at Dwaling, north-east of Oatbarton. Albin Northcotton asked you to venture to Dwaling and let them know the farmer's market will be opening early this year.\n",
[5048]="700359A5\n1\tFarm hardy bulbs for the folk of Wildermore (quantity: see journal)\tThe recipe for hardy bulbs (both field and crop) has been given to you by Hildelith. You should farm hardy bulbs for the folk of Wildermore.\n2\tDeliver the hardy bulbs to Hildelith\tHildelith is in Forlaw. You have crafted Hardy Bulbs and should now deliver them to Hildelith.\n",
[5049]="7002F453\n1\tClaim your tickets to the Farmers Faire\tA Festival Announcer can be found in the centre of Bywater during the Farmers Faire festival. You should speak with her to claim your free Festival Tickets!\n",
[5050]="7002AF48\n1\tWait for the game to begin\t'You should head into the field shortly. We will be trying to find some of those delicious mushrooms growing out there...but be careful: once Farmer Maggot notices us out in the field, he will surely sic those dogs of his on us. You need to stay away from them! 'Come back here once you've eaten your fill of mushrooms.' This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n2\tDevour mushrooms (total: 5)\tGather at least five mushrooms. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n3\tGather more mushrooms\030Avoid Maggot's dogs\tYou have succeeded in devouring five of Maggot's mushrooms...eat as many more as you can before the game is over!\n4\tTalk to Osbert Puddifoot\tTalk to Osbert Puddifoot to receive your tokens for winning the Mushroom Hunt.\n",
[5051]="7002AB17\n1\tWait for the game to begin\tSandson's Egg Scramble will begin shortly. Your goal is to collect at least five white eggs -- but you can earn additional tokens by collecting extra eggs... and especially for collecting the rare coloured eggs! Wait in the chicken yard until Wymarc Grubb declares the game underway. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n2\tCollect white eggs (total: 5)\tGather five white eggs as quickly as you can. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n3\tGather more eggs\tYou have succeeded in gathering five white eggs -- get as many more as you can before the game is over. You should try to grab any festive eggs that you spot.\n4\tTalk to Wymarc Grubb\tTalk to Wymarc Grubb to receive your tokens for winning the Egg Scramble.\n",
[5052]="7000978B\n1\tDefeat swarming locusts (total: 8)\030Defeat locust-queens (total: 4)\030Find anything amiss in Nibs Chubb's fields\tNibs Chubb's fields are east and north-east of his farm. Nibs Chubb has accepted your offer of aid and has pointed you towards his fields.\n2\tTalk to Nibs Chubb\tNibs Chubb is at his farm, east of Oatbarton. You should return to Nibs Chubb and tell him of the elk-carcass and the wolf that attacked you.\n",
[5053]="7002E563\n1\tBring the Tokens of Hytbold to Fréamar\030Gather Tokens of Hytbold (quantity: see journal)\tThere is much work to do to rebuild the town of Hytbold.\n",
[5054]="7002E5A9\n1\tBring the Tokens of Hytbold to Fréamar\030Gather Tokens of Hytbold (quantity: see journal)\tThere is much work to do to rebuild the town of Hytbold.\n",
[5055]="7002E5AC\n1\tBring the Tokens of Hytbold to Fréamar\030Gather Tokens of Hytbold (quantity: see journal)\tThere is much work to do to rebuild the town of Hytbold.\n",
[5056]="7002E593\n1\tBring the Tokens of Hytbold to Fréamar\030Gather Tokens of Hytbold (quantity: see journal)\tThere is much work to do to rebuild the town of Hytbold.\n",
